<title>USA: BOXING-LOPEZ KEEPS TITLE IN SURPRISINGLY TOUGH FIGHT.</title>
<headline>BOXING-LOPEZ KEEPS TITLE IN SURPRISINGLY TOUGH FIGHT.</headline>
<dateline>LAS VEGAS 1997-03-29</dateline>
<text>
<p>Ricardo Lopez of Mexico made his 19th consecutive title defence of the World Boxing Council strawweight title by beating Mongol Charoen of Thailand in a unanimous decision on Saturday.</p>
<p>Lopez was given every round by judges Carol Castellano and Martin Sammon, 120-107, and judge Joraicio Castillo had it 119-108.</p>
<p>Lopez is 45-0. Charoen dropped to 17-2.</p>
<p>Lopez has held the title since 1990 the longest of any reigning champion.</p>
</text>
